Z||000004||Cheever2||08-08-2001||12:38 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroMaster88:<BR><B>Official program???  How much? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>James: I have to ask $20 for it, but that will include shipping.  It's in excellent condition.  I got it from "Indy500nut" on eBay.  My home puter's down, but email me at chodges@litton.c-bass.com if you want it and I will see your email tomorrow evening.<P>8Ball: thanks for the info.  I found it... <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1174694170" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1174694170</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 08-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||08-08-2001||09:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroKyle:<BR><B>Hey, what was the engine used to power the real pace cars cuz that iron duke by its self isn't fast enough to pace indy cars with out mods. Also did the Fiero just pace the Indy cars for one year?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was powered by a 2.7L SD4 engine. You can still buy an SD4 engine but a 232hp street version is close to $9000.00. There are a few places to get used SD4's. I looked into getting one that was local to me but the guy wanted $6500.00 for the 232hp version and $12,000.00 for the 282hp race engine.<BR>They are nice engines and will make a Fiero fly. But with the high cost of the engines,<BR>You could do a swap with a bigger/more HP engine and still have change left.<P>The Fiero paced Indy only in 1984 but the 2 PPG pace cars paced a few IMSA races each year until 1987. (don't think they did any in 1988 due to the announcement of the stopping of the production cars)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||peterh||08-08-2001||03:51 PM||||I was at the Chicago Museum of Science and Industry last month and they had an original Indy pace car. It was behind a glass enclosure so could not see much, but it looked good with the wide fenders and snorkel.<P>||||reg||1
